  "//overrides": "Each answers a bun audit advisory on transitive dev tooling (#1931) and is held within the range its parent asks for: browserslist GHSA-73wf-gq98-2v4g and GHSA-c83g-rgw3-j3cx (react-docgen's @babel/core, which still asks ^4.24.0), valibot GHSA-5qjj-4xww-7phc (@storybook/addon-mcp), and postcss GHSA-fxqj-rqcc-2cmp (the copy @tailwindcss/postcss nests, which still asks ^8.5.16). Drop each once its parent ships the fix itself: baseline-browser-mapping (browserslist now asks ^2.11.26, past GHSA-w5vr-8v7q-w6rv) and nanoid (postcss now asks ^3.3.19, past GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8) are gone for that reason. The pins that only the story runner needed went with @storybook/test-runner (#2907): the jest and @jest/* block, uuid, joi, axios and js-yaml came in through its jest, nyc and wait-on tree, and the playwright and playwright-core pins kept its own copy on the @playwright/test version (#737). The story tests run on vitest through @vitest/browser-playwright, which takes the one playwright that @playwright/test already pins, so there is nothing left to pin; bun run check:playwright-pin fails if the lockfile ever holds a second copy.",
